KG42.register("source_edge_archive-eaac599c3f1b23a27723ace1",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::E::v141-c-R005-E001","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-36e0a27c810a788e","target":"KG31-c38847500f58498d","source_occurrence_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::V::execution.energy_trade","source_unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"6d11eef40c8e95ae856b0ce93cdf26d9586a39436c9bce101a26c85c37761f39","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Each prosumer submits its chosen next-slot energy-consumption quantity x_n^o to the MGO. Scope: Hour-ahead ESM within the microgrid; submission of each prosumer's chosen total consumption for the next time slot. The MGO is obligated to pursue maximization of its own profit when coordinating PV energy sharing. Scope: The MGO's objective in the Stackelberg energy-sharing arrangement. The MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance supplies and demands. Scope: The microgrid operator's external balancing duty under ESM. Condition: An internal mismatch occurs between PV power generation and load power demand. A server should be deployed in the MGO. Scope: Infrastructure at the MGO for implementing ESM. Condition: Implementation of the ESM.","target_definition":"The prosumer must sell its net surplus to the MGO, which purchases seller energy at the internal selling price p_s. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0 Under the source's nonpositive-net-energy branch, the prosumer must buy its net energy requirement from the MGO, which sells buyer energy at the internal buying price p_b. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The prosumer must sell its net surplus to the MGO, which purchases seller energy at the internal selling price p_s. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0","expression":"\\forall n\\in G:\\; E_n^g - x_n > 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\bigl(E_n^g - x_n \\text{ is sold to the MGO at } p_s\\bigr)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x-x_n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-theta-E_n^g","v141-c-R005-theta-p_s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Under the source's nonpositive-net-energy branch, the prosumer must buy its net energy requirement from the MGO, which sells buyer energy at the internal buying price p_b. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0","expression":"\\forall n\\in G:\\; E_n^g - x_n \\le 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\bigl(x_n - E_n^g \\text{ is bought from the MGO at } p_b\\bigr)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x-x_n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-theta-E_n^g","v141-c-R005-theta-p_b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.B Profit Model of MGO","anchor_text":"( n n) ( ) act n∈B ave Es = (Egn −xn). (4) n∈S 0 In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosum","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"]},"paper_scope_note":"Stackelberg ESM, deviation billing, and the Cournot baseline are kept separate; buying/selling branches, numerical cases, and the no-deviation/penalty conditions are retained with the declaration."}});
